<html>
<title>Settings</title>
<body>

<h1>Settings</h1>

<p>
<img src="images/menu_settings.png" border="0" width="326" height="272">
</p>


<h2>Wav File and Real Cassette Settings</h2>

<p>
Open the window to change settings for WAV files and <a href="ComputerRealCassette.htm">Real Cassette Support</a>.
</p>


<h2>Equalization</h2>

<p>
Select one of the submenu items to adjust sound equalization. By default, <strong>TV Speaker</strong> is selected. See the <a href="ComputerSound.htm">Sound</a> section.
</p>

<h2>Window</h2>

<p>
Select one of the submenu items to control the Emma 02 <a href="MainWindow.htm">Window</a>.
</p>


<h2>CPU Type</h2>

<p>
<img src="images/menu_cpu.png" border="0" width="433" height="272">
</p>

<p>
Select one of the submenu items (1) to choose the CPU type used for all emulated computers. By default, <strong>CDP1805</strong> is selected, allowing a more extensive instruction set than the <strong>CDP1802</strong>. The <strong>CDP1805</strong> is backward compatible with the <strong>CDP1802</strong>, which was used in most emulated computers.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> The <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/fred1.html">FRED 1</a> will always be emulated using a <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/system00.html">SYSTEM00</a>, and the <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/microtutor.html">Microtutor</a>, <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/coin_arcade.html">RCA Video Coin Arcade</a>, <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/fred1_5.html">FRED 1.5</a>  and <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/fred3.html">FRED 3</a> will always be emulated using a <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/1801.html">CDP1801</a>. This is because these CPUs were used in the original machines and are not fully compatible with the <a href="https://www.emma02.hobby-site.com/1802.html">CDP1802</a>.
</p>


<h2>Startup Values</h2>

<p>
<img src="images/menu_startup.png" border="0" width="459" height="272">
</p>

<p>
Select one of the submenu items (1) to set the startup values for CPU registers, RAM, or Video RAM. The following options are available:
</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Zero</strong>: CPU registers, RAM content, or Video RAM content is set to 0 at startup</li>
<li><strong>Random</strong>: CPU registers, RAM content, or Video RAM content is set to a random value at startup</li>
<li><strong>Dynamic</strong>: RAM content or Video RAM content is set similar to COMX dynamic RAM content at startup. This content is a repeating pattern of 64 values of 255 (FF) followed by 64 values of 0. One random location within these 128 values will contain a random value instead of 0 or 255.</li>
</ul>


<h2>Function and Hot Keys</h2>

<p>
Open the <a href="MainFunctionKeys.htm">Function and Hot Keys</a> window.
</p>


<h2>Use Numeric Keypad</h2>

<p>
Deselect this menu item if your PC does not have a numeric keypad (<tt>Numpad</tt>). If unselected, all keymap definitions will, where possible, not use any key definitions from the PC numeric keypad.
</p>

<h2>Default Keyboard</h2>

<p>
<img src="images/menu_keyboard.png" border="0" width="474" height="368">
</p>

<p>
The default keyboard mapping is defined for a US keyboard layout. However, several other layouts (Dutch, German, French, Swedish / Finnish) are provided and can be selected via this menu. See the <a href="MainKeyMappingDefault.htm">Default Keyboard</a> section.
</p>

<h2>COMX SuperBoard</h2>

<p>
Only used in the COMX and COMiX emulators if a <a href="MainComxSb.htm">COMX SuperBoard</a> is configured. The popup menu allows selection of <strong>Online</strong>, <strong>USB</strong>, and <strong>Backup</strong> settings.
</p>

<p>
For more information about the Super Board (SB) project, see the <a href="https://www.comx35.com/superboard.html">COMX Super Board</a> website.
</p>

</body>
</html>

